# OWNER REVIEW
# The club's sessions (WO-014b, DESIGN.md "The Velvet Claw's house"; levels/hub/club_life.gd, core/club_game.gd).
# A waiting client's check-in with Nim (in the suit; in her garb, the dress code), and the sisters' aftercare.
# Content lines: suggestive, clothed (swimwear at most), consensual: a check-in before, aftercare after, and the
# safeword always heard. The kink is never the joke; a hypocrite in a false moustache can be.

~ client_garb
Client: Are you one of the Mistresses? ...Oh. Not in those. Not tonight, then.
[narrator] Sessions are in the suit. The members' wardrobe is upstairs, by the door.

~ client_suit
Client: Mistress? I was hoping someone would be free.
Nim: Tell me what you'd like.
Client: To be tied up and told what to do. Something soft. Nothing sharp.
Nim: And if it gets to be too much?
Client: My word's "pineapple". And "yellow" if I need you to slow down.
Nim: Pineapple. Yellow. Good. Come with me.
- Begin. => client_go
- Not tonight. => client_later

~ client_go
set club/session_go
=> END

~ client_later
Client: Another time, then. I'll be here.

~ smith_garb
Smith: I am not here. This is not me. Good evening.

~ smith_0_suit
Smith: Ahem. I am, er, Mister... Smith. A private citizen. Of no political affiliation whatsoever.
Nim: Your moustache is coming off.
Smith: It's a very relaxed moustache.
Smith: I'd like to be scolded. Thoroughly. For hypocrisy, ideally. I have so much of it.
Nim: And your word?
Smith: "Decency." I never use it otherwise. Ha. Ha ha.
- Begin. => client_go
- Not tonight. => smith_later

~ smith_later
Smith: Quite right. I was never here.

~ pip_garb
Pip: Oh! Hi. Sorry. I thought you were... never mind. Hi.

~ pip_0_suit
Pip: Hi. Sorry. Hi. It's my first time. Is that obvious?
Nim: A little. That's fine. What would you like?
Pip: I don't know. Something gentle? I want to find out if I like it.
Nim: Then we'll go slowly, and you'll tell me. Your word?
Pip: Um. "Teacup"? Is that silly?
Nim: Teacup's perfect. And "yellow" to slow down. I'll be watching for it.
- Begin. => client_go
- Not tonight. => pip_later

~ pip_later
Pip: That's okay. I'll just... sit. And watch. If that's allowed.

# --- the regulars' stories (levels/hub/club_life.gd: "<who>_<visit>_suit" before, "<who>_after_<visit>" after a good
# session; four visits each, then "<who>_done_suit") ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Mr Smith: a Coalition man in a false moustache. The hypocrite's the joke, never the kink. Over four visits he
# works out who he's been marching with, and hands Nim the Coalition's committee roll (flag intel/coalition_roll).
# Pip: a nervous first-timer who finds out they like it here. Over four visits Pip gets brave, becomes a member, and
# leaves Nim a teacup (flag keepsake/teacup).

~ smith_after_0
Smith: Same time next week. I shall deny it, of course. Vigorously. In print.

~ smith_1_suit
Smith: Ahem. Mister Smith. Again. The moustache is new. Different moustache. Entirely different man.
Smith: The Coalition had a meeting about "establishments like this" today. I took notes. For research.
Nim: What did they decide?
Smith: To shut you down. Then they had sherry. Then I came here. I'd like to be scolded about that, please.
Nim: Your word's still "decency"?
Smith: I've never needed it less.
- Begin. => client_go
- Not tonight. => smith_later

~ smith_after_1
Smith: The Chairman's pamphlets are printed somewhere off Press Alley. Not that I know that. Not that I said it.
Smith: Good evening. I was never here. Again.

~ smith_2_suit
Smith: I forgot the moustache. I noticed on the stairs. I found I didn't much care.
Smith: There's a man who brings plush toys to the Coalition's meetings. Pale blue. A spiral on the tummy. Everyone gets one.
Nim: ...Go on.
Smith: After the session. I'd like to feel I've earned telling you.
- Begin. => client_go
- Not tonight. => smith_later

~ smith_after_2
Smith: The toys come from a Mr Swyne. The Chairman calls him "our benefactor". Everyone who has one goes very quiet.
Smith: I've been marching beside him for a year. Decency. Ha. I'd like a drink, and then I'd like to think.

~ smith_3_suit
Smith: I've resigned. Well. I've written the letter. I'll post it after this, if I'm brave.
Smith: Same as always, please. Firmly. I've a lot of hypocrisy left to work off and I'd like to be done by spring.
- Begin. => client_go
- Not tonight. => smith_later

~ smith_after_3
[narrator] Mr Smith takes a folded paper from his robe pocket and holds it out, without the moustache, without a joke.
Smith: The Coalition's committee roll. Every name. Swyne's is pencilled in beside the Chairman's.
Smith: Give it to whoever you work for. I think I know who that is. I think I've always rather admired her.
set intel/coalition_roll
Nim: Thank you, Mr Smith.
Smith: Gerald. It's Gerald. ...No, keep calling me Mr Smith. I've grown fond of him.

~ smith_done_suit
Smith: Gerald Smith, private citizen, no affiliations, and the lightest he's felt in years. The usual?
- Begin. => client_go
- Not tonight. => smith_later

~ pip_after_0
Pip: That was... I liked that. I really did. Can I come back? Is that allowed?

~ pip_1_suit
Pip: I came back! I brought a list. Is a list weird? It's a short list. It's mostly "gentle" written three times.
Nim: A list's perfect. Same word?
Pip: "Teacup". Still not silly.
- Begin. => client_go
- Not tonight. => pip_later

~ pip_after_1
Pip: I told my sister I'd joined a book club. She asked what we were reading and I said "rope". I panicked.

~ pip_2_suit
Pip: I want to try the... um. The flogger? Gently? I watched Silke and it looked like weather. Nice weather.
Nim: Gently, then. And "teacup" if it isn't nice weather.
- Begin. => client_go
- Not tonight. => pip_later

~ pip_after_2
Pip: I think I'm braver in here than anywhere. Isn't that strange? It's the safest place I know.

~ pip_3_suit
Pip: They made me a member! Bastion nodded at me. Bastion! He's never nodded at anyone. I nearly fainted.
Pip: One more, for the occasion. Then I've got something for you.
- Begin. => client_go
- Not tonight. => pip_later

~ pip_after_3
[narrator] Pip presses a teacup into Nim's hands: bone china, a little chipped, a rose painted on the side.
Pip: It's my teacup. You know. The word. I thought you should have it.
set keepsake/teacup
Nim: I'll keep it safe.
Pip: Lull says she'll put it on her shelf. With the important things.

~ pip_done_suit
Pip: Hi! Member Pip, reporting. Is "reporting" right? Gently, please. I've a list.
- Begin. => client_go
- Not tonight. => pip_later

# --- the sisters, afterwards ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

~ silke_switch_after
[narrator] Silke works the last knot loose and rubs Nim's wrists, slowly, one and then the other.
Silke: How was that?
- Quiet. Good quiet. => silke_after_good
- Strange. Good strange. => silke_after_good

~ silke_after_good
Silke: Mm. Water. Sit a while. Don't stand up fast.
Silke: You breathe well. Nobody teaches that.

~ silke_switch_red
[narrator] Silke has the rope off in three pulls, and a blanket round Nim's shoulders in a fourth.
Silke: Red. Good. You said it, I heard it. That's the whole thing.
Silke: Nothing's wrong. Sit with me.

~ silke_domme_after
[narrator] Nim unties her. Silke flexes her hands, looks at the knots, and nods.
Silke: Not bad. Your third was lazy.
Silke: ...I liked it. Ask me again sometime.

~ silke_domme_red
[narrator] Nim has the rope off before Silke finishes the word.
Silke: Fast. Good. Nothing wrong, just enough. Thank you.

~ augusta_switch_after
Augusta: There. Sit. Tea's coming. You held that far longer than you think you did.
Augusta: Most people fight their own shoulders. You let them go. Lovely.

~ augusta_switch_red
Augusta: Red. Good girl. Sit down, darling, sit. That's exactly what it's for.

~ augusta_domme_after
Augusta: Well. I've been corrected by worse. Your "shoulders down" wants more conviction.
Augusta: ...And you asked how I was. Do keep doing that. It's the best part.

~ augusta_domme_red
Augusta: Thank you for stopping the instant I said it. That's all the conviction anyone needs.

~ grizelda_switch_after
[narrator] Grizelda turns one boot to the light, then the other.
Grizelda: Adequate. ...Better than adequate. Up. Off your knees. Water.
Grizelda: You were careful. People think I want fast. I want careful.

~ grizelda_switch_red
Grizelda: Red. Up. Sit. That was right, and I'm not cross. I'm never cross about that.

~ grizelda_domme_after
[narrator] Grizelda gets up off her knees as if she'd chosen to, and takes the water Nim holds out.
Grizelda: You waited for the right moment every time. Hm.
Grizelda: You may sit on my throne again. Rarely.

~ grizelda_domme_red
Grizelda: You stopped. Good. Don't fuss. ...Fuss a little.

~ lull_switch_after
[narrator] Lull slips the blindfold off and lets the light come back slowly.
Lull: There you are. How do you feel?
- Far away. Nicely. => lull_after_good
- Heavy. In a good way. => lull_after_good

~ lull_after_good
Lull: Mm. Stay that way a while. Tea's here when you want it.

~ lull_switch_red
Lull: Red. Blindfold's off. I'm right here. Nothing's wrong; you just knew.

~ lull_domme_after
[narrator] Nim lifts the blindfold. Lull blinks, smiling at nothing.
Lull: I never knew where you'd be. That's a gift, you know.
Lull: Sit with me. My turn to pour.

~ lull_domme_red
Lull: Thank you. That was enough, that's all. You were lovely about it.

~ dash_switch_after
[narrator] Dash flops onto the floor, and pats the floor beside her.
Dash: You're fast! Not as fast as me. But fast!
Dash: Water. Both of us. Then stretch. Then probably more water.

~ dash_switch_red
Dash: Red! Stopping! Stopped! Good. Sit, sit. I went too fast, didn't I. Thanks for saying.

~ dash_domme_after
[narrator] Nim lets go. Dash stays exactly where she is, for once.
Dash: You held on. Nobody holds on.
Dash: ...Okay, that was really good. Don't tell Grizelda I said "really".

~ dash_domme_red
Dash: Red. Thanks. I meant it, see? Even laughing. Good stop.

~ rivet_switch_after
[narrator] Rivet unbuckles each cuff and turns it over in her hands, checking the wear.
Rivet: Fit's good. You've got narrow wrists; I'll take a notch out of the next pair.
Rivet: You told me the truth every time. That's the useful kind of sub.

~ rivet_switch_red
Rivet: Red. Off they come. Something pinched? Tell me what and I'll fix the design.

~ rivet_domme_after
[narrator] Rivet flexes her wrists in the cuffs, then holds them out to be undone.
Rivet: Every buckle checked. You've no idea how rare that is.
Rivet: ...Thanks. I could get used to someone else being careful for once.

~ rivet_domme_red
Rivet: Off. Good. Quick hands. I'll remember that.
